From: McKack <4465550+McKack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:26:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] airconv: non-indexed draws through a geometry shader

The vertex stage of a geometry shader pipeline took the index buffer path for non-indexed draws: index_buffer_idx is ~0u when there is no index buffer, and the check tested it for non-zero, so it read a function argument that doesn't exist and the compile failed. Ghostrunner (UE4, D3D11) rendered only its HUD.
---
 src/airconv/dxbc_converter_gs.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/airconv/dxbc_converter_gs.cpp b/src/airconv/dxbc_converter_gs.cpp
index d554ba6..dafc43f 100644
--- a/src/airconv/dxbc_converter_gs.cpp
+++ b/src/airconv/dxbc_converter_gs.cpp
@@ -790,7 +790,7 @@ convert_dxbc_vertex_for_geometry_shader(
       builder.CreateBr(finalize_index);
     }
 
-  } else if (index_buffer_idx) {
+  } else if (index_buffer_idx != ~0u) {
     auto start_index = builder.CreateExtractValue(draw_arguments, 2);
     auto index_buffer = function->getArg(index_buffer_idx);
     auto index_buffer_element_type = index_buffer->getType()->getNonOpaquePointerElementType();
